 align="center">12.0 &#x02013; 35.0</td></tr><tr><td></td><td align="center">24</td><td align="center">3.06***</td><td align="center">85</td><td align="center">DIK2568</td><td align="center">-0.103</td><td align="center">0.587</td><td align="center">0.005</td><td align="center">71.1 &#x02013; 97.1</td></tr><tr><td></td><td align="center">26</td><td align="center">2.11*</td><td align="center">63</td><td align="center">OARJMP23</td><td align="center">0.042</td><td align="center">0.480</td><td align="center">0.038</td><td align="center">50.0 &#x02013; 62.5</td></tr><tr><td colspan="9"><hr></hr></td></tr><tr><td align="center">BW98</td><td align="center">11</td><td align="center">3.10***</td><td align="center">29</td><td align="center">HEL10</td><td align="center">NA</td><td align="center">0.870</td><td align="center">NA</td><td align="center">29.3 &#x02013; 46.3</td></tr><tr><td></td><td align="center">23</td><td align="center">2.15*</td><td align="center">71</td><td align="center">URB0031</td><td align="center">NA</td><td align="center">0.843</td><td align="center">NA</td><td align="center">22.5 &#x02013; 83.0</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p>BW<italic>xx </italic>is the body weight at week <italic>xx</italic>; models fitted are of the form 'Sex + QTL + Sex.QTL', except for week 98 (wethers only) for which the model was 'QTL' only; <italic>P</italic>-values were obtained from likelihood ratio tests (LRT) with 2 df (testing QTL + Sex.QTL) or 1 df (QTL only, in Week 98); these <italic>P</italic>-values were adjusted for false discovery using the method outlined in Benjamini and Hochberg [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B42">42</xref>] with *<italic>P </italic>&#x0003c; 0.05, **<italic>P </italic>&#x0003c; 0.001, ***<italic>P </italic>&#x0003c; 0.005, ****<italic>P </italic>&#x0003c; 0.0001; standardized QTL effects are expressed as the estimated effect difference (Awassi &#x02013; Merino) relative to the estimated residual standard deviation</p></table-wrap-foot>